**Given:**

The man covers a distance in three different parts.

The speed of the man for three different part is 35 km/hr, 8 km/hr, and 18 km/hr respectively.

**Concept:**

Average speed = {Total distanceover Total time}

**Formula used:**

S={Dover T} Where, S = Speed, D = Distance, and T = Time

**Calculation:**

Let the total distance is D

Time taken in first travel = {{Dover 2}over 35} = {Dover70}

Time taken in second travel = {{{40over 100}times {Dover 2}}over 8}={Dover40}

Time taken in third travel = {{{60over 100}times {Dover 2}}over 18}={Dover60}

The total time taken by man = {Dover70}+{Dover40}+{Dover60}={12D+21D+14Dover840}={47Dover840}

The average speed = {Dover {47Dover840}}={840over47} km/hr

**∴ The required result will be {840over47} km/hr.**
